{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>A prophet from among you, from your brothers, like me.</b> This is said about Joshua, which is why He said to him, 'you shall hearken,' and we find concerning Joshua that it is written (Joshua 22): ״וישמעו אליו בני ישראל״. Or, 'a prophet' may be in the plural, and the reason He needed to say 'like me' is so that you would not understand from the word 'your brothers' the children of Esau or the children of Ishmael, since we find regarding the children of Esau (Numbers 20): ״כה אמר אחיך ישראל״; therefore He added and said 'like me,' meaning from the children of Jacob, and this refutes the faith of Ishmael, for prophecy is not found among them. And there are four things that no nation merited but Israel alone, and they are: prophecy, the Torah, the land of Israel, and the resurrection of the dead, and in the parashah of וזאת הברכה I will mention this with the help of the Blessed One, for there the three are mentioned. And furthermore, 'like me' — that he should hold fast to my ways, that he may neither add nor subtract nor uproot any commandment from the commandments of the Torah, unless he be an established prophet and only for the time being; but to uproot a single commandment entirely, one does not hearken to him. For our faith in the prophecy of Moses is not on account of his signs and wonders, such that you would say, 'do I then believe in Moses only because of his signs? — here too are signs.' Rather, our firm faith in the true prophecy of Moses is not because of the signs and wonders He performed for us, but because we ourselves heard the discourse from the mouth of the Almighty along with him, and through this the truth of his prophecy was established and clarified for us, for we know the matter and are witnesses to it. And Scripture explains this matter, namely what the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses (Exodus 19): ״הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן בעבור ישמע העם בדברי עמך וגם בך יאמינו לעולם״. Thus explained the Rambam, of blessed memory."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:22.417632457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}